# Attack speed cap (server/README.md "Attack speed cap"): life / mana leech rolls on every hit, so more hits per second
# meant more healing per second. Three rules, each a config.lua number (0 turns it off; the defaults below apply when
# config.lua does not name it), readable from Lua as configManager.getNumber(configKeys.<KEY>):
#  1. minPlayerAttackInterval = 1000: no player swings faster than once per 1000 ms, whatever the vocation, the weapon,
#     its Chaos attack speed modifier and topaz gems (data/lib/chaos_item_mods.lua M.syncAttackSpeed) and dexterity.
#  2. maxPlayerAttackSpeedBonus = 25: every attack speed bonus together (the weapon's attribute against its type's own
#     interval, or 2000 without one; the stat window's dexterity) shortens the vocation-scaled interval by at most 25%.
#  3. minPlayerLeechInterval = 900: life leech heals at most once per 900 ms, mana leech too (each its own timer). A roll
#     inside the window is skipped. Covers every extra hit at once: the Ninja off-hand, Bloodrage and keystone cleaves,
#     ricochets and echoes, Flurry, pets / companions / minions hitting as their owner, support repeats.
# Also: dexterity is clamped to 0..100 (a value above 100 made the interval negative). Lua mirror of rules 1 and 2:
# ChaosItemMods.effectiveInterval (tests/attack_speed_cap_test.lua), shown as "Your Attack Interval" in item tooltips.
# Apply in the server source root after 0001-0010: patch -p1 < 0011-attack-speed-cap.patch, then rebuild.
